\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves rise after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2011\par 02:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Y692.5 bln \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifts \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves\par \par \uc2  * Rise in euro vs dollar lifts value of euro-denominated assets\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to seek continued G7 cooperation after joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the Japanese economy click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2  By Kaori Kaneko\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves rose in March after it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem a sharp rise in the yen after the earthquake and tsunami, pulling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  away from a record peak against the dollar.\par \par \uc2  The reserves rose to $1.12 trillion at the end of March compared to $1.09 trillion at the end of February, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2  Japan used a total of 692.5 billion yen ($8.1 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, when Group of Seven (G7) countries joined it in their first joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in more than a decade after the yen shot to a record 76.25 yen to the dollar. [ID:nL3E7EV1T3]\par \par \uc2  The yen has extended its losses since the rare coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and market players say the broader trend points to a continuation of yen weakness given growing expectations that the Bank of Japan will lag central banks in the euro zone and the United States in raising interest rates.\par \par \uc2  On Thursday the yen fetched around 85.40 yen to the dollar, near a six-month low, and 122.30 yen to the euro , near an 11-month low. \par \par \uc2  "There has been a clear difference in direction among major central banks' interest rates. The possibility of more joint G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has greatly declined, given the yen's weakness on interest rate differentials," said Hideki Hayashi, a global economist at Mizuho Securities.\par \par \uc2  "Since the G7 members have stuck to their stance of cooperating if needed, I wouldn't rule out more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen rises sharply. But the possibility is small considering the market situation at the moment." \par \par \uc2  Japan plans to seek continued cooperation from the G7 countries at a meeting next week when the group's finance chiefs meet in Washington. G7 sources told Reuters this week that the economic impact of Japan's triple disaster of earthquake, tsunami and nuclear crisis will be high on their agenda. [ID:nN04252436]\par \par \uc2  Tokyo had last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on its own on Sept. 15, 2010, when it used 2.13 trillion yen, a record amount for a single day.\par \par \uc2  Announcing the latest figures for Japan's reserves, the ministry said gains in the euro against the dollar contributed to pushing up the dollar-based value of euro-denominated assets.\par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.4158 at the end of March, compared with $1.3806 at the end of February. ($1 = 85.475 Japanese Yen) \par \par \uc2 (Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY-RESERVES/UPDATE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110407e74700010\par }\page {\par\fs20