\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ: Yen's Fall Seen Continuing;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen Working\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alex Frangos  \par \uc2 Of THE WALL STREET JOURNAL  \par \uc2 1,078 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2011\par 18:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's fall to its lowest level against the dollar and the euro in months is the latest sign that a coordinated post-earthquake \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is working.\par \par \uc2 But how low can the yen go?\par \par \uc2 The dollar was buying more than Y85 during the Asian trading day Wednesday. That amounts to a 7% decline for the yen since the Group of Seven industrialized nations announced a coordinated bout of yen selling March 18, and its weakest level since September, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on its own.\par \par \uc2 In early U.S. trading Wednesday, the dollar was at Y85.34, up from Y84.83 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at Y121.89 from Y120.64. A day before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was at around Y78.95 and the euro was at around Y110.70.\par \par \uc2 "This is shaping up to be one of the most successful episodes of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ever," says Sean Callow, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Westpac Institutional Bank in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 The euro hit an 11-month high against the yen in Asia Wednesday, thanks to the increasingly divergent paths being set by monetary authorities in the two economies. The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to raise interest rates at a meeting Thursday. Higher interest rates generally attract capital.\par \par \uc2 The yen's steady drop in recent weeks is encouraging the view that a turning point could finally be at hand for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after more than two years of strengthening against the dollar that has frustrated Japanese companies and politicians.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at Nomura say the break of 85 yen "could be significant from a medium-term perspective and we would not be surprised to see a trend of further yen weakness." Nomura has revised its forecast to reflect a further drop in the yen, predicting that the dollar will be buying more than Y90 in 2012 as U.S. interest rates rise and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's remain anchored.\par \par \uc2 The success of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is partly explained by traders who now see a ceiling on yen strength, thanks to the threats of future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That's given investors confidence to pile into so-called carry-trade bets, in which they borrow yen at very low interest rates and convert that cash into higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Australian dollar, which is also trading at recent highs against the yen.\par \par \uc2 Another factor is Japan's weakened economic condition. Rolling electricity blackouts and nuclear fears are hampering manufacturing and exports. Even a temporary disruption could lessen the demand for Japanese automobile, technology and machinery companies to convert money earned abroad back into yen.\par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered dropped its 2011 Japan growth forecast from 1.9% to 0.7% this year. It raised its 2012 forecast in expectation of a strong V-shaped recovery, and figures the dollar will strengthen to Y90.\par \par \uc2 Meantime, the Bank of Japan was scheduled to meet Thursday and is under pressure to further loosen monetary conditions by expanding its asset-purchase program to support Japan's post-earthquake recovery, a move that would naturally depress the yen by increasing its supply.\par \par \uc2 A weaker yen should aide embattled Japanese companies coping with the aftermath of twin natural and nuclear disasters, and continued supply and electricity shortages.\par \par \uc2 Hitachi Ltd\uc2 . President \uc2 Hiroaki Nakanishi\uc2  said Wednesday that the dollar trading above 85 yen is a "more natural state." He said that Hitachi designed its budget for the fiscal year that just began this month based on the expectation that the dollar would trade at 80 yen.\par \par \uc2 "For us, it would be favorable if the dollar remained stable in the 85 yen to 90 yen range," he said.\par \par \uc2 The head of Japan's leading big business lobby welcomed the weakening of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , describing it as a return to normality.\par \par \uc2 "The yen is finally back to where it was" six months ago, said Hiromasa Yonekura, chairman of the Nippon Keidanren, noting that "intrinsically, the yen was at the 90 to 100 yen level before the Lehman shock," a reference to the global financial crisis that followed the collapse of U.S. investment bank \uc2 Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc\uc2 . in the fall of 2008.\par \par \uc2 While mostly welcomed, a much weaker yen could complicate Japan's rebuilding by making energy and commodity imports more expensive, a situation noted Tuesday by the country's economy minister Kaoru Yosano.\par \par \uc2 "With the recent yen weakening, high oil prices could hit the economy directly," Yosano said. Japan imports more than four million barrels of oil per day. And its badly damaged nuclear infrastructure suggests it will have to rely on other forms of fuel such as natural gas and coal, which will also need to be imported.\par \par \uc2 The long-term success of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to be measured in months and years, rather than weeks. A stronger yen could resurface, as it did after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  unilaterally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in September. After an initial weakening, the yen rebounded, growing stronger than at the initial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  point within a few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, not everyone is expecting the yen to slide. \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  continues to recommend clients bet on a stronger yen versus the dollar, figuring the dollar will dip back below Y80 in coming quarters thanks in part to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistent trade and current account surpluses.\par \par \uc2 The coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been successful despite governments' swapping relatively small amounts of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Japan disclosed recently it used 692.5 billion yen on March 18, compared with 2.1 trillion yen in the September \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Canada has said it sold around $124 million in yen March 18. The U.K. sold about $150 million worth.\par \par \uc2 "There's been lots of failures over the years. It's looking very impressive," says \uc2 Westpac\uc2 's Callow.\par \par \uc2 Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are increasingly rare. But they also have a tendency to be successful, though economists question whether it is the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that cause a change in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's direction or other more-powerful underlying factors, such as trade flows and interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the euro in 2000 and in the yen in 1995 and 1998 all had the effect of marking long-term or medium-term changes in direction for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at play.\par \par \uc2 -By Alex Frangos, The Wall Street Journal; alex.frangos@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 --Chester Dawson, Yoshio Takahashi and Juro Osawa contributed to this article. [ 04-06-11 1258ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110406e746000e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
