\par\par \b \uc2 DJ FOCUS: Interest Rates Tighten Grip On  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Flows\b0\par\par\uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2011\par 05:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Calmer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets feed shift out of low-interest-rate \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- But uncertainties could easily scupper bets\par \par \uc2 By Siva Sithraputhran OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--A familiar trading trick seems to be returning to the market as investors start selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  linked to low interest rates, and gravitating instead towards those backed by higher yields.\par \par \uc2 This strategy, called the carry trade in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market speak, was widespread before the financial crisis, and seems to be making a slow return as wider concerns about the knock-on effects of the March 11 earthquake in Japan and the continuing troubles in the Middle East recede and as greater attention turns to monetary policy in the big economies.\par \par \uc2 'The change in \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric towards a more hawkish bias from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of England and lately by the Fed, is working its way into \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market dynamics,' said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Credit Agricole, in a research note.\par \par \uc2 This, along with improved appetite for riskier assets is 'very bullish for high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but also proves bearish for low yielders,' and explains the current burst of yen weakness and strength in the likes of the Australian dollar, he added.\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2  strategist Geoffrey Yu said that the bank 'strongly supports the view that the carry trade has turned a corner' but cautioned that investors shouldn't lose sight of other related factors.\par \par \uc2 Strengthening the case for the carry trade, expectations of big swings in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates have been hugely reduced by a series of policy measures across the world, Yu said.\par \par \uc2 These measures include injections of liquidity in Europe and the U.S. and, in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's case, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 But on the other hand, market perceptions could be shaken and lead to sharp movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, jeopardizing the carry trade, Yu said. 'Fed and ECB policy positions--also key carry drivers--could shift fundamentally this month,' he added.\par \par \uc2 The ECB is this week widely expected to deliver its first rate increase since 2008 and the tone of its post-verdict comments will be scrutinized for clues about whether the rise will be the first of many, as some are predicting. The Fed, meanwhile, will have to decide whether it will scale back its supply of cheap cash to the system. Both may yet produce surprises.\par \par \uc2 Other analysts were less convinced that the time is ripe for investors to pile back into the carry trade. They argue that the yen has played a strong role as a refuge during times of uncertainty and any fresh increase in investor nerves could easily propel the yen higher, making it risky to bet against the yen.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the yen's current weakness is at least partly the result of other factors. Japanese funds and companies have sent home far less money than expected in response to the earthquake speculation is now receding that such flows will ever come flooding in. Also notable is the Swiss franc's strength despite low interest rates in Switzerland.\par \par \uc2 Paul Robson, strategist at \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 , said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements in line with predictions on interest rates are only to be expected, but that doesn't necessarily mean that carry trades are back on. 'I'm not sure there is enough risk appetite in the market.'\par \par \uc2 Adam Cole\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 , echoed this view. 'I'm not convinced that this is a theme yet,' he said, adding that he is even less certain whether the yen would be the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice to be sold.\par \par \uc2 'The yen is not uniquely low yielding, there are lot of alternative low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the G10,' he said and cited the U.S. and Canadian dollars as well as the euro and sterling as possible alternatives.\par \par \uc2 -By Siva Sithraputhran, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9462; (siva.sithraputhran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110407e7460048u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
