\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UK Spent Just $150M In G-7  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Weaken Yen Mar 18\b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2011\par 11:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Amount spent symbolic\par \par \uc2 --BOJ keeping powder dry\par \par \uc2 By Siva Sithraputhran\par \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 London (Dow Jones)--The U.K.'s part in the concerted efforts to tame the yen's strength on March 18 amounted to just $150 million (Y12 billion), data released by the U.K. Treasury revealed Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after the Group of Seven nations agreed on a rare joint campaign to tame the yen as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shot to record highs following the Japanese earthquake. The dollar hit a record low of Y76.25 on March 17, and the March 18 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  succeeded in pushing it back up to Y82, providing the foundations for further gains through the month.\par \par \uc2 Many traders had assumed at the time that the amounts involved in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were huge, with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling rumored to be around Y2 trillion, matching the amount it sold in a similar move in September last year.\par \par \uc2 However, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last Thursday it spent Y692.5 billion to weaken the yen. Data from the other central banks that also sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not yet available.\par \par \uc2 Analysts attribute the success of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the gravity of the statement from the G-7 which had followed a period of intense speculation.\par \par \uc2 Geoff Yu, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2 , said the tiny U.K. amount was "symbolic and to show solidarity with the Bank of Japan."\par \par \uc2 The contribution of the other central banks would also have been for small amounts, Yu said, adding that the total spend would have been larger if the cash had originated from the Bank of Japan.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at Nomura said in a note last week that the small amount spent by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  "does not mean that Japanese authorities' appetite for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is any less than it was in September."\par \par \uc2 They believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the dollar reaches the Y80.0 level and there is a significant decline in stock prices.\par \par \uc2 Nomura analysts noted that Japan' budget for the new fiscal year, which was passed 29 March, raised the ceiling for spending on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Y36.9 trillion. "With the endorsement of G-7 nations, Japanese authorities have substantial room to prevent yen appreciation if necessary, in our view," they said.\par \par \uc2 -By Siva Sithraputhran, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0)20 78429462; siva.sithraputhran@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 05, 2011 05:58 ET (09:58 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110405e74500216\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
