\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : China Rate Increase Rattles Market\b0\par\par\uc2 1,106 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2011\par 13:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Aussie dollar dented by China rate move\par \par \uc2 --Wider impact from China move likely to be fleeting\par \par \uc2 --Case for higher UK rates boosts pound\par \par \uc2 --Euro-zone data weigh on euro\par \par \uc2 --U.S. ISM awaited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Siva Sithraputhran \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--China's quarter-point interest rate increase midway through the European trading session took markets by surprise, sending the Australian dollar lower and depressing the euro slightly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  raised benchmark lending and deposit rates by 25 basis points when Hong Kong and Chinese markets were closed for a public holiday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the timing of the increase was a surprise, the move itself was widely expected as China tries to tackle inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There has been an impact but it is small and I suspect it will be fleeting," said Jane Foley, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar, seen as a key gauge for any slowdown in China, fell on the news but the effect is likely to pass as the Aussie's prospects hasn't suffered much, she said. "Markets have become more accustomed to these moves and this hike won't be the last this year," Foley added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Aussie had been weakening after data showed an unexpected trade deficit in Australia and after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left interest rates unchanged.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Separately, the pound got a lift from a key survey showing unexpected strength in the services sector which forms the bulk of the U.K economy, taking the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to its highest level against the dollar since March 24.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The data suggests that the U.K's first quarter performance may prove stronger than expected, in turn strengthening the case for a Bank of England rate increase. The services Purchasing Managers Index rose to 57.1 in March from 52.6 in February, research group Markit and the Chartered Institute of Purchasing and Supply said. Economists had expected the services PMI to stay at 52.6.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Strong March survey data and by implication growing upside risk to [growth] are at the root of pound strength," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adam Cole\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of England will deliver its interest rate verdict Thursday but the chances of higher interest rates just yet are very slim.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro meanwhile has been on the back foot through the European session as investors take a breather after having driven the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher on expectations that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift interest rates Thursday. Those expectations remain intact but investors are now more concerned on the outlook for rates beyond Apr. 7.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The day's European data were mixed with services sector PMIs beating expectations slightly while retail sales were weak. Taken together, they weighed on the euro slightly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking ahead, the U.S. ISM non-manufacturing index is due at 1400 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Consensus is for a little changed headline reading at 59.5, but the index has surprised to the upside in each of the last six months," said Cole at \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2 , suggesting that the dollar may perk up further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback got a boost late Monday after remarks acknowledging inflation from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Separately, data released by the U.K. Treasury revealed Tuesday that the U.K.'s part in the concerted efforts to tame the yen's strength on March 18 amounted to just $150 million (Y12 billion).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came after the Group of Seven leading industrial nations agreed on a rare joint campaign to tame the yen as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shot to record highs following the Japanese earthquake. The dollar hit a record low of Y76.25 on March 17, and the March 18 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  succeeded in pushing it back up to Y82, providing the foundations for further gains through the month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many traders had assumed at the time that the amounts involved in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were huge, with the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rumored to have sold around Y2 trillion, matching the amount it sold in a similar move in September last year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Geoff Yu, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said the tiny U.K. amount was "symbolic and to show solidarity with the Bank of Japan."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The contribution of the other central banks would also have been for small amounts, Yu said, adding that the total spend would have been larger if the cash had originated from the Bank of Japan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at Nomura said in a note last week that the small amount spent by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "does not mean that Japanese authorities' appetite for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is any less than it was in September."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 They believe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again if the dollar reaches the Y80.0 level and there is a significant decline in stock prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nomura analysts noted that Japan's budget for the new fiscal year, which was passed 29 March, raised the ceiling for spending on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to Y36.9 trillion. "With the endorsement of G-7 nations, Japanese authorities have substantial room to prevent yen appreciation if necessary, in our view," they said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was at $1.4165 from $1.4220 late Monday in New York, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at 84.33 from Y84.06, while the euro was at Y119.47 from Y119.52. The U.K. pound was at $1.6234 from $1.6127. The dollar was at 0.9239 from CHF0.9233.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index was at 76.00 from 75.904 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1142 GMT     1.4165     84.39      1.6224     0.9241 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish    Bullish    Bullish    Range \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Bullish    Bearish    Range \par 200 day ma        1.3552     84.06      1.5831     0.9775 \par 3rd Resistance    1.4251     85.00      1.6318     0.9341 \par 2nd Resistance    1.4232     84.73      1.6295     0.9295 \par 1st Resistance    1.4191     84.49      1.6249     0.9255 \par Pivot*            1.4227     84.09      1.6137     0.9229 \par 1st Support       1.4145     84.17      1.6090     0.9205 \par 2nd Support       1.4125     83.80      1.6015     0.9192 \par 3rd Support       1.4061     83.20      1.5973     0.9126 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/GBP \par  \par Spot 1142 GMT     119.54 \par 3 Day Trend       Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish \par 200 day ma        0.8559 \par 3rd Resistance    0.8823 \par 2nd Resistance    0.8800 \par 1st Resistance    0.8770 \par Pivot*            0.8815 \par 1st Support       0.8720 \par 2nd Support       0.8690 \par 3rd Support       0.8655 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Siva Sithraputhran, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 20 7842 9462; siva.sithraputhran@dowjones.com [ 05-04-11 1110GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110405e745000rk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
