\par\par \b \uc2 DJ 2nd UPDATE: BOJ March Tankan Doesn't Fully Reflect Quake Impact\b0\par\par\uc2 1,101 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2011\par 05:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --BOJ tankan's headline business sentiment index at 6 in March, compared with 5 in the previous December tankan\par \par \uc2 --23.6% of participating company responses were received after the earthquake hit eastern Japan on March 11\par \par \uc2 --BOJ will release post-quake indexes on Monday morning\par \par \uc2 (Adds economist comments and background on the earthquake.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Megumi Fujikawa \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Not taking into account the impact of the massive earthquake and tsunami that struck northeast Japan on March 11, or the subsequent nuclear emergency, the Bank of Japan's closely watched tankan survey released Friday showed Japanese business sentiment improved slightly in March.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But in a highly unusual move, the BOJ said it would separately release the indexes for responses gathered after the quake at 8:50 a.m. local time on Monday (2350 GMT Sunday). Those data are expected to give a more somber perspective on the Japanese economic outlook, and analysts say the results could prod the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to loosen its monetary policy further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Friday's data, the main index of large manufacturers' business sentiment for the three months to March improved to 6, compared with 5 in the previous December tankan and the median 7 forecast by economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires. The figure represents the percentage of companies saying business conditions are good minus those saying conditions are bad.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sentiment among large non-manufacturers also rose to 3 in March from a reading of 1 in December and economists' forecast of 2.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  considers the tankan a key source of information when formulating monetary policy, but Friday's results may not be the best indicator of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy direction as it reflects almost none of the impact from the earthquake and the following spike in the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The data only confirms that the economy was set to emerge from the lull before the earthquake," said Yoshiki Shinke, senior economist at Dai-Ichi Life Research Institute, adding that various economic indicators due later will likely force the BOJ to ease monetary policy further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Of the 11,101 companies surveyed by the BOJ from Feb. 24 to March 31, 23.6% of the responses were received after the earthquake, although they may have reflected views prior to the quake. The latest tankan's recommended deadline for responses was the very day of the temblor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday's supplementary figures are expected to offer a more somber view on Japan's economic perspective, although those companies most affected may still not be counted in the results. Possibly reflecting the widespread disruption to quake-hit regions, the overall response rate for the survey was 95.6%, down from the usual response rate of nearly 99%. Though, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday's data should be used for "reference purposes only."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some analysts expect Monday's outcome to prod Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to take further action as early as at its two-day policy-setting meeting starting Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Monday release will be the first data collected by the Bank of Japan that reflect the impact of the disaster, which could increase the chances of additional easing at their meeting later next week," said Kenro Kawano, chief fixed-income strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Japan. He expects the bank to increase the amount of asset purchases or possibly reduce the interest rate on reserves from the current 0.1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Such action could have a positive effect on markets, Kawano said, even though its direct impact on the economy would be hard to gauge.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Three days after the quake, the BOJ quickly jumped into action, doubling its asset purchase program to Y10 trillion to prevent a deterioration in firms' and households' sentiment. It has also supplied ample liquidity to the short-term money market amid increasing concerns about the ability of banks to meet a surge in demand for funds from companies and households.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After next week's meeting, the board will again meet to review its semiannual forecasts for the economy and prices April 28.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking ahead, the March tankan shows big manufacturers predicted business sentiment will deteriorate to 2 in the next survey in June, while large non-manufacturers expect their sentiment index to be at minus 1. But the indexes are expected to deteriorate even more sharply in the next survey as the impact of the recent disasters will likely become clearer in the coming months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The headline diffusion index will probably drop sharply to a negative double digit number," said Masamichi Adachi, economist at JPMorgan Securities Japan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While heavy damage at the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant is only one negative factor among serious power outages and supply chain disruptions, the course of events with the facility in the coming months will be one key to overall sentiment, Adachi said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The increased uncertainty makes it very easy for firms to scale back their capex, so what happens over the next three months will be crucial for the Japanese economy," Adachi said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Big manufacturers and non-manufacturers plan to lower capital spending by 0.4% in the new fiscal year beginning Friday, the tankan showed. That compared with a 1.6% rise expected by economists. March figures are usually downbeat because many companies had yet to map out new capital investment plans at the time of the tankan poll.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, big-sized companies have a nearly flat outlook for their profits for this fiscal year. Large manufacturers forecast a climb of 0.6% after a 59.0% rise in the previous business year. Big non-manufacturers expect an 0.4% profit decline after a 22.3% climb.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The surveyed companies' latest profit forecasts are based on the dollar averaging Y84.20 this fiscal year, compared with a previous projection in December of Y86.47, the tankan showed. If the yen strengthens, earnings generated overseas could shrink significantly when repatriated into Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Following rare joint action by Japan and its Group of Seven counterparts to weaken the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yen has stabilized to a large extent. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  conducted yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  March 18 after the dollar fell to a new post-war low of Y76.25 the previous day. The pair stood at Y83.66 as of 0253 GMT Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Toko Sekiguchi, Takashi Mochizuki, Tatsuo Ito, Andrew Monahan and Kosaku Narioka contributed to this article\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 31, 2011 23:08 ET (03:08 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110401e741000nb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
