\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  portion of G7 yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  Y692.5 bln--MOF\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 14:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  thought to have done most part of G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more effective than unilateral action\par \par \uc2 * Exact total size of G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  not known\par \par \uc2 (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted a total of 692.5 billion yen ($8.4 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, when Group of Seven (G7) countries conducted their first joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in more than a decade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen has since eased back to around 82.80 yen to the dollar , compared with a level of 79.50 yen just before Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said on March 18 that the G7 had agreed to step in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The day before that, the yen hit a record high of 76.25 yen.\par \par \uc2 The data only covers \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the total size of the G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still not known, although many market players think \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  did most of the job.\par \par \uc2 But the joint move appears to be working more effectively than \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, when it sold a record 2.12 trillion yen to stem a rise in the yen.\par \par \uc2 "The announcement effect of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was effective, making the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more efficient," said Teppei Ino, an analyst at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.\par \par \uc2 The data does not specify which \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were bought and sold but market players said the Bank of Japan bought the dollar against the yen.\par \par \uc2 The release from the Finance Ministry simply said the total amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the period from February 25, 2011 through March 29, 2011 was 692.5 billion yen.\par \par \uc2 That amount was not too far off market players' estimates of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of around 530 billion yen, give or take a few hundred billion yen that had been based on BOJ money market data.\par \par \uc2 Those estimates were based on several assumptions, including one that all the yen settlements related to G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cleared with the BOJ, which some analysts say may not be the case.\par \par \uc2 Also, if a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  finances its yen selling by selling Japanese short-term bills or bonds, the BOJ data may not capture the flows because the data only shows net, and not gross, yen payments to banks from the public sector, including foreign central banks.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Hideyuki Sano; Editing by Edwina Gibbs)\par \par \uc2 (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110331e73v000wc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
