\par\par \b \uc2 No Reason To Doubt G-7 Would  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  Again On Yen-Europe Official\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laurence Norman   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 15:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS (Dow Jones)--The Group of Seven leading nations would likely be prepared to repeat their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen appreciation if needed, a senior European official said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the G-7 carried out what is thought to have been large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record high of Y76.25 following the Japanese earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 The G-7's yen selling was effective in blunting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. The dollar was at Y82.36 at 1250 GMT Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The official, who participated in the work leading up to the G-7 decision, said "the Japanese have the impression that if needed, we would do it again," he said of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "That's also my view," he said.\par \par \uc2 The official said that when the idea of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  was first discussed by the G-7, "nobody had major objections or strong reasons why it should not be done."\par \par \uc2 He said there were some who doubted the effectiveness of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempt but they were won around.\par \par \uc2 "I don't see any reason why it would not be done again," he said.\par \par \uc2 The official said he wasn't aware of any follow-up discussion at G-7 level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the action was announced March 18.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it wouldn't hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets again in the case of excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 -By Laurence Norman, Dow Jones Newswires; 32-2741-1481; laurence.norman@dowjones.com [ 03-29-11 0948ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110329e73t0008i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
