ECB President Trichet on Monday said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on track to hike rates in April, re-focussing some traders' attention on interest rate differentials which are in favor of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The euro is at 1.4080, from 1.4087 late Monday in New York, the EUR/JPY is at 115.10, from 115.12, and the USD/JPY is at 81.74, compared with 81.67. On the data front, South Korea has February BOP data at 2300 GMT, Japan releases February household spending and February jobless reports at 2330 GMT, and February preliminary retail sales data at 2350 GMT. Later, St. Louis Fed President Bullard speaks in Prague, the U.S. releases January S&P/Case-Shiller Home Price Index, March consumer confidence and the weekly API gasoline and crude stocks data. (shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments and share their views on financial news topics. Please email us at:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TalkBackAsia@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2255 GMT [Dow Jones] New Zealand's February trade surplus of NZ$194 million shows high commodity prices continue to support export values although there is some evidence of moderation in world prices, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Philip Borkin. "Looking forward, the outlook for NZ's trade balance is naturally heavily dependent on the performance of soft commodity prices and global demand," he says. Exports totaled NZ$3.87 billion in February vs NZ$3.3 billion in January. Borkin adds imports are also likely to increase in the near term as businesses replace stock damaged in the February earthquake. (lucy.craymer@dowjone