\par\par \b \uc2 Specter Of More G-7  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Keeps Dollar-Yen Steady\b0\par\par\uc2 895 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 21:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -After coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders less likely to tempt fate\par \par \uc2 -"No reason for stealth" - analyst\par \par \uc2 -More overt tactics seen after transparency grabbed market's attention\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Andrew J. Johnson \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Last week's coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem a surge in yen strength may have changed the way traders look at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -led \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , making them far less likely to tempt fate and challenge Japanese officials than in the past.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar has remained remarkably steady against the yen this week in the aftermath of last Friday's Group of Seven nations' coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . This Friday, the dollar finally broke out of its tight range, rising by 0.6% against the yen, to Y81.44--the direction the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prefers to see.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is impossible to say how the MoF would coordinate a new effort to thwart another sudden strengthening of the yen, but if anything, the new effort is likely to be as loud and coordinated as last time, said several market participants.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "[There is] no reason for stealth," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 David Woo\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of global rates and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "The reason why dollar-yen is so stable is because the market respects the [last] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and does not want to take on the Bank of Japan--and the G-7--together."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To be sure, market participants aren't completely ruling out the possibility that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could act alone on further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But there are strong reasons to think otherwise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prior to last Friday, if history had been a guide, traders could have expected the unexpected on future \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts, as the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely aimed to keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market participants on their toes, by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at different levels, at different times of the global day and perhaps even going it alone.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the game changed last Friday, said those participants, because Japanese officials have to be pleased with the success of the far-more-overt and mass-coordinated effort. As such, they will likely stick with what worked and adopt that as their new strategy, said the participants.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A key reason why this type of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have been effective, so far, isn't the size of the effort, but rather the intimidation factor of so many central banks working together to move the market, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last Friday by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and its G-7 partners probably amounted to about Y530 billion, according to BOJ data and market estimates of fund flows, a far smaller figure than the roughly Y2 trillion some traders had previously estimated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By contrast, over the course of the global day on Sept. 15--the previous occasion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market--the finance ministry sold Y2.12 trillion for dollars. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  acted alone in that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is really the transparency of the new effort that seems to have grabbed the market's attention the most, the market participants said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The G-7's communique last week said the group "will join with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , on March 18, 2011, in concerted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in exchange markets." The G-7's emphasis on a specific date left some market participants and even Japanese government officials with the impression that the group hadn't committed to further yen-selling beyond March 18.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the communique is just vague enough that traders are reluctant to expect the G-7 group wouldn't again act in concert, said the market participants. "The statement that stands is strong, and unless that changes, I don't expect the dynamic to change," said Andrew Wilkinson, senior market analyst at Interactive Brokers in Greenwich, Conn. "There is limited upside potential to be long yen, [and] anybody who pushes the envelope risks provoking the wrath of the G-7."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That public warning shot from the G-7 on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was significant and effective, said Willie Williams, director of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  institutional sales at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 , because the MoF isn't really trying to swim against the tide and weaken the yen to an unrealistic degree. They are just trying to scare the market and prevent shocking surges upward like last week, in which the yen leapt to new record highs against the dollar, he said. Disorderly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets can destabilize other markets including stocks, which the MoF would want to avoid.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They are not [particularly] worried about yen strength: They are concerned about the pace of the yen's strength," Williams said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The G-7 group members closed ranks after the yen hit an all-time high last Thursday of Y76.25 to the dollar--fueled in part by thin trading after New York equity markets closed and electronic trading likely accelerated the move. The yen's spike also came after a devastating earthquake and tsunami, which clouded the country's economic outlook.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank officials could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at an unexpected level, allowing the dollar to slip as low as Y77-Y78, so as to keep in place the element of surprise, said Jens Nordvig, head of G-10 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at Nomura Securities in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the "line in the sand" on further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely sits around the Y80 mark, most said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew J. Johnson, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-3092; andrewj.johnson.com [ 03-25-11 1639ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110325e73p000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
