\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECT: WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Pares Gain On Debt Concern But Finds Support\b0\par\par\uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 08:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ("WORLD \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Euro Pares Gain On Debt Concern But Finds Support," at 0533 GMT, misidentified the euro as the dollar in the fifth paragraph. The correct version follows:)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    By Tatsuo Ito \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The euro pared earlier gains against the dollar in Asian trading Thursday as concerns over sovereign debt problems in the euro zone prompted traders to take profits, but the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found support as traders here downplayed the risk that the European debt woes will keep worsening.\par \par \uc2 "It isn't a situation where the European debt problem will continue to worsen. So the euro is unlikely to fall further," said Dai Sato, vice president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2 . Portugal's parliament rejected on Wednesday new budget curbing measures proposed by Prime Minister Jose Socrates, who immediately tendered his resignation. "The news itself did not have a lasting impact here as the outcome was mostly anticipated," Sato added.\par \par \uc2 During morning trade, the euro fell against the dollar on an Expansion report in its Internet edition Thursday that \uc2 Moody's\uc2  will downgrade the credit ratings of Spanish banks today. The euro was further dragged down by comments from a Swedish official on the likelihood of a "number" of banks failing the forthcoming EU stress test. Swedish FSA Official Lars Frisell tells Dow Jones "there will be a number of banks failing the stress test."\par \par \uc2 "Despite various pieces of euro-negative news, it is fairly well-bid on expectations of a rate hike by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," says Yoshio Yoshida, a trader at Mizuho Trust and Banking.\par \par \uc2 At 0450 GMT, the euro was $1.4085 compared with $1.4086 late Wednesday in New York, according to EBS. The dollar was at Y81.02 from Y80.91. The euro was Y114.08 from Y113.96.\par \par \uc2 Regarding dollar/yen trade, Mizuho Corp's Sato said "dollar-buying incentives are scare after its upside test ended in failure on Wednesday, with most Japanese players now refraining from building up fresh positions before their book-closing" at the end of this month.\par \par \uc2 The downside for the greenback was supported by persistent concerned about a possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen.\par \par \uc2 "Speculators are refraining from taking aggressive shorts on the dollar due to fears of another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with dollar sales being limited to commercial operators like importers," said Osao Iizuka, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at \uc2 Sumitomo Trust\uc2  and Banking.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, continued uncertainty over the problems at Japan's Fukushima nuclear plant kept a lid on the dollar's gains.\par \par \uc2 "It looks odd to see the yen come under upward pressure on negative plant-related news, but risk-aversion sentiment is stronger than such bad news," coupled with a fall in Tokyo share prices, Iizuka said.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was 75.95 from 75.927.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily 