\par\par \b \uc2 G7  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  gives go-ahead for yen carry trade\b0\par\par\uc2 851 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 12:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen boosting yen carry trades\par \par \uc2 * Aussie and kiwi dollars to be supported by flows in April\par \par \uc2 * BOJ seen last in normalising monetary policy\par \par \uc2 By Anirban Nag\par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 23 (Reuters) - The Group of Seven \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive down the yen has created conditions ideal for the Japanese yen to become the preferred funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and this could boost growth-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Australian dollar.\par \par \uc2 In their first joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000, G-7 rich countries sold the yen <JPY=> on Friday after it spiked to record highs of 76.25 per dollar and threatened to deal a blow to the export-reliant Japanese economy that was just picking up from a lull when the earthquake and tsunami struck.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan is not expected to drain yen that enter the market through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nTKZ006879] In addition, the BOJ eased its ultra-loose policy even further last week, taking a step further away from rate normalisation.\par \par \uc2 The flow of yen into the financial system, ultra-low Japanese money market rates and expectations yen gains will be capped should combine to see the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  take over from the U.S. dollar as the world's preferred funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Positive risk appetite, expectations that Japanese money market rates will remain low, and the (fact the) Bank of Japan will likely counter any repatriation flows mean conditions are supportive for yen-funded carry trades," said Hans-Guenter Redeker, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In carry trades, investors borrow in a lower yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to invest in others which return higher yields to investors. In the past two years as the global economy recovered from the financial crisis, the bulk of carry trades used the dollar as the funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yen-funded carry trades were very common before the global financial crisis struck in mid-2008, having picked up after the BOJ unilaterally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2004 to drive the yen lower. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 TIMELINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market [ID:nTOE673024]\par \par \uc2 G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sub68r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sub68r}}}\par \par \uc2 Reuters Insider show on G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  [ID:nRTV202021] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 Since Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Australian dollar <AUDJPY=R> has gained 5.9 percent against the yen to a peak of 81.90 yen from 77.34 yen. The return of Japanese investors could push the Aussie to revisit its highs of $1.0257.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, the New Zealand dollar has advanced to 60.04 yen from a near two-year low of 54.98 struck on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The action in the kiwi dollar at a time not much is going in favour of the New Zealand economy shows that there is an opportunity out there and yen-funded carry trades could become attractive," said Steve Barrow, head of G-10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Standard Bank.\par \par \uc2 APRIL FLOWS\par \par \uc2 Australia's benchmark interest rate is 4.75 percent, while New Zealand's cash rate is at 2.5 percent, amongst the highest in the rich world where the Federal Reserve, the Bank of England and the Bank of Japan all have rates near zero.\par \par \uc2 In contrast to the Australian and New Zealand dollars, the U.S. dollar has struggled to hold on to its gains against the yen <JPY=> made after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Still, most expect the G7 to sell more yen and see 80.00 yen as a line in the sand.\par \par \uc2 Traders say ahead of Japan's March 31 fiscal year end there has also been a marked rise in Japanese commercial and retail interest to buy yen. Once that is over, April will bring with it a surge in Japanese investor sales of the yen, with upside risk in the yen all but absent.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are confident that the G7 won't let the yen go below 80 versus the dollar again," said David Cohen, director of Asian forecasting at Action Economics, Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "That makes the carry trade appealing and will restore investors' interest." He said Japanese retail investors who were pulling back last week would return to buy high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, data from Tokyo Financial Exchange show Japanese retail margin traders have been trimming their long positions in Aussie/yen. On Monday, net longs fell by 20,250 lots, compared with a huge 88,429 lots on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Overall, Japanese margin traders have cut their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying to a two-week low. Their buying of seven major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen fell to 398 billion yen ($4.91 billion) on Tuesday, down more than 300 billion yen from a record net long of 732 billion yen last Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say with the Federal Reserve likely to end quantitative easing in June, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely to raise interest rates next month and the Bank of England considering rate hikes in the second quarter, Japan will be exceptional in holding rates near zero.\par \par \uc2 "With the Fed likely to move ahead of the BOJ, carry trades which were being funded in the dollar will move to the yen," said Barrow at Standard Bank.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /CARRY   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110323e73n000mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
