\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 926 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: BOJ SIGNALS COMFORT WITH LIQUIDITY, ON BOARD WITH YEN-WEAKENING EFFORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan skipped its money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday morning, the first time it has refrained from pumping extra cash into the banking system since the devastating March 11 earthquake and suggesting it is--so far--leaving the yen from Friday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par *\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOVT: SEES MAXIMUM Y25 TRILLION IN DAMAGE FROM QUAKE AND TSUNAMI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (published 0554 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ MIYAO: TO CONSIDER POLICY OPTIONS TO HELP POST-QUAKE RECONSTRUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan policy board member Ryuzo Miyao suggested Wednesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may set up a special facility to help revive areas affected by a massive earthquake and tsunami that struck northern Japan on March 11. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ MIYAO CAUTIONS OVER ECONOMIC IMPACT OF QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan policy board member Ryuzo Miyao on Wednesday cautioned that the economic impact of the massive earthquake that hit the country on March 11 is likely to be significant, and said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stands ready to ensure stability in financial markets. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOKYO METROPOLITAN GOVT: IODINE EXCEEDING PERMISSABLE LEVELS FOR INFANTS DETECTED IN TAP WATER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Tokyo Metropolitan Government said Wednesday that iodine exceeding permissible levels for infants has been detected in tap water in northern Tokyo. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: LOW JGB YIELDS REFLECT CONFIDENCE IN FISCAL REFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Wednesday that low Japanese government bond yields reflect market confidence in the country's fiscal reform efforts. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC YI: INFLATION PRESSURES BUT NO CHANGE IN CPI NUMBERS - REUTERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A People's Bank of China deputy governor said China's facing inflationary pressures but is confident his country would be able to keep a CPI rise pegged at 4% this year, Reuters reported Wednesday. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: 2011 YUAN APPRECIATION TO EXCEED 5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan is certain to appreciate more than 5% this year, in line with widespread expectations and many economists' forecasts, a Chinese government economic researcher said Wednesday. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN TO INTRODUCE CARBON PRICE LEGISLATION IN SPRING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia will introduce legislation for its planned carbon tax in the Spring sitting of parliament, Treasurer Wayne Swan said Wednesday in a statement. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN EXPORTERS WARN GOVERNMENT ON PLAN TO PRICE CARBON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Representatives of two major Australian exporting industries Wednesday warned the government to take special care in imposing a price on carbon. (published 0350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : GRADUAL RATE HIKES CAN CONTAIN DOMESTIC DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday said it agreed at its March 9 policy board meeting that gradual interest rate increases remain sufficient to contain domestic demand, but warned that fiscal stimulus after an upcoming general election could accelerate inflationary pressure. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: NZ'S WIDER CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT RAISES RATING CONCERNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's current account deficit for the three months to Dec. 31 widened significantly from the preceding period due to higher import costs and increased earnings for foreign investors with assets in New Zealand, and the data raises further concerns about the economy's health, which could trigger a downgrade for the country's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  credit rating. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND FINANCE MINISTER: APRIL 1 TAX CHANGES WILL HELP REBALANCE ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Bill English said Wednesday that tax changes that will come into effect April 1 will further rebalance New Zealand's economy towards savings and exports. (published 0157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par G-20 MULLING GIVING IMF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SWAP MANDATE FOR CENTRAL BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund is working on a proposal to become a more significant lender of dollars, euros and other hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during times of crisis, essentially sharing the role of global lender of last resort with the U.S. Federal Reserve. (published 2247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPE COULD WITHSTAND YIELD SURGE, ECONOMIC SLUMP - S&P STUDY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A surge in bond yields and a sharp economic downturn would weaken the creditworthiness of western European countries and have "severe social costs" in Greece, Ireland, and Portugal, with nearly one-quarter of borrowers in these countries and Spain defaulting, although western Europe as a whole could withstand the shock, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS OFFERS S$2.5 BILLION OF APRIL 2016 GOVT BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore has invited bids for a S$2.5 billion offering of five-year government bonds that is expected to settle on April 1. (published 0150 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: YANLORD LAND PRICES $400 MILLION DOLLAR BOND AT 10.625% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yanlord Land Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . priced its seven-year global dollar bond offering to yield 10.625%, the Chinese property developer said in a statement to Singapore Exchange Wednesday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par PREVIEW: SINGAPORE FEBRUARY INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY UP 6.3% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in Singapore's manufacturing output likely slowed in February as the benefits of a low base of comparison wore off and the Lunar New Year holidays cut the number of working days. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FOCUS: IN BAHRAIN, POLITICAL UNREST THREATENS FINANCE HUB AMBITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bahrain's ambitions to establish the Persian Gulf kingdom as a leading regional financial center are under threat amid escalating unrest in the tiny island state, giving neighboring hubs in Doha and Dubai an edge in their bid to lure international financial institutions to their shores. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 23-03-11 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI00