\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 683 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 16:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par US FEBRUARY NEW HOME SALES FALL TO RECORD LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sales of new homes plunge to a new record low, sinking 16.9% to a seasonally adjusted rate of 250,000 in February, and prices fall to the lowest level in more than seven years. Economists were expecting sales to rise 2.1% to a rate of 290,000.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FED REJECTS BANK OF AMERICA DIVIDEND, CAPITAL PLAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve rejects a plan submitted by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2  in the latest round of Fed stress tests that would have 'modestly' increased its dividend this year. The bank says it intends to resubmit a comprehensive plan in the summer. Shares dip more than 2%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALLIES STRAIN TO MEND SPLIT OVER LIBYA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A coalition of military powers pound the Gadhafi regime's military installations for a fifth day and solidified their control over Libya's skies -- even as they continued to struggle to resolve an internal conflict over how to lead the campaign.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCKS STILL DOWN AFTER WEAK NEW HOME SALES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks remain lower after U.S. new home sales fall to a record low. Investors also focus on continuing violence in North Africa and the Middle East, and consider the possible collapse of Portugal's government.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NY FED TO LAUNCH NEW REVERSE RPS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York\f28 \uc2 \f2  will launch a new round of small reserve repo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday, a move designed to drain reserves from the system. The Fed says the move isn't meant to signal any shift in Fed monetary policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERNATIONAL MARKETS POWER \f28 \uc2 \f2 GENERAL MILLS\f28 \uc2 \f2  PROFIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Mills\f28 \uc2 \f2  fiscal 3Q earnings rise 18% of $392.1 million, or 59c a share, as the maker of cereals, Progresso soups and Hamburger Helper says that profit soared at its international business. Shares fall 3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLDMAN'S BLANKFEIN TAKES STAND IN GALLEON TRIAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lloyd Blankfein\f28 \uc2 \f2  takes the witness stand for the government at the insider-trading trial of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Galleon Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  founder Raj Rajaratnam.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COLGATE TO BUY UNILEVER UNIT FOR $940M \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 World's largest toothpaste maker agrees to buy the Sanex personal-care brand from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unilever\f28 \uc2 \f2  for $940 million, or EUR672 million, strengthening its personal-care business in Europe.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SIGNALS COMFORT WITH CURRENT LIQUIDITY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  refrains from pumping extra overnight funds into the banking system for the first time since the devastating earthquake on March 11, and left the yen from the coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday in the market.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAKES PROGRESS ON NUCLEAR PLANT CONTROLS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vital control and cooling systems are expected to come back online in the next few days at some of the most damaged reactors of the quake-hit Fukushima Daiichi nuclear complex, Japan's nuclear safety agency says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ACTRESS ELIZABETH TAYLOR DIES AT 79 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hollywood actress Elizabeth Taylor, famed for her striking beauty and a film career that spanned five decades, has died in a hospital in Los Angeles, according to a statement by her publicist. She was 79 years old.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET \par Singapore Exchange Should Look At "Plan B" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With his proposed $8.3 billion tieup with the Australian exchange facing increasingly stiff political opposition the Singapore Exchange's chief executive, Magnus Bocker, should probably look more closely at his "plan B," Sam Holmes writes.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS \par Time To Short The Yen Is Nigh \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This could finally be the time to take up short positions in the yen. The G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday may have helped to halt the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rally, but the loss of haven status as well as post-quake policies will likely ensure the yen turns down.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ============ U.S. MARKETS ACTION =========== \par DJIA              down 29.41 points to 11988.81 \par NASDAQ            down 17.17 points to 2666.68 \par S&P 500           down  7.33 points to 1286.44 \par 10-year T-note    102 26/32 at 3.2902 yield \par NYMEX Crude       up $0.65 at $105.62/bbl \par Dollar/Euro       down 0.0040 at 1.4143 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-23-11 1102ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 5030 55101   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110323e73n000ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
