\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: BOJ Data Suggest Friday's  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Totaled About Y530 Bln\b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 12:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background in paragraphs five and six)\par \par \uc2 By Hiroshi Miwa\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its Group of Seven partners likely amounted to about Y530 billion, according to Bank of Japan data and market estimates of fund flows, a far smaller figure than the roughly Y2 trillion some traders had previously estimated.\par \par \uc2 BOJ flow of funds data released Tuesday showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects a net Y60 billion to flow into Japan's money market Wednesday, when the transactions from Friday's coordinated G-7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are set to settle. Excluding the effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market players estimate there would have been a net outflow of Y470 billion.\par \par \uc2 That suggests that the G-7 authorities likely sold about Y530 billion in Friday's action to driven down the yen after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared to a record high against the dollar a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 Japan was closed for a national holiday on Monday. The yen transactions will settle in Japan's money market.\par \par \uc2 A Japanese government source said last Friday evening that speculation that Japanese monetary authorities sold Y2 trillion during Tokyo trading hours was "groundless."\par \par \uc2 Over the course of the global day on Sept. 15--the last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market--the finance ministry sold Y2.12 trillion for dollars. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted alone in that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Hiroshi Miwa, Dow Jones Newswires; +813 6269 2800; hiroshi.miwa@dowjones.com [ 22-03-11 1131GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110322e73m000y3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
