\par\par \b \uc2 AT A GLANCE: Japan Makes Further Progress On Nuclear Crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 08:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THE NEWS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a sign of further progress at the stricken Daiichi nuclear power plant, authorities said that they have now connected electricity to another reactor, this time the No. 4 unit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 That means that normal electricity is now in the process of being made available to five of the six units, although workers are moving cautiously in testing the plant infrastructure before restoring full power to the control systems and cooling systems of each unit.\par \par \uc2 The only unit not yet connected is Unit 3, considered the most problematic, where overhead spraying continues to try to cool the pool that holds spent fuel. The spraying missions by fire departments from Tokyo and Osaka have helped in lowering temperatures in the spent fuel pools to keep them from catching on fire.\par \par \uc2 Discoveries of higher-than-normal radiation levels in outlying areas also continued to be reported, with Kyodo news service quoting officials from \uc2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\uc2 . (9501.TO) as saying that iodine-131 has been found at sea 16 km away from the facility.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MARKET REACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The progress in the recovery work has helped to stabilize nervous \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. The dollar is at Y80.90 in late Asian trading compared with Y81.01 late Monday in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks surged on reconstruction hopes following the devastation wrought by the earthquake and tsunami, with the Nikkei 225 stock average closing up 4.4% at 9608.32.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CASUALTIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's national police agency said the number of people killed by the earthquake and tsunami as of 0300 GMT Tuesday was 9,079, with 12,645 missing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires' coverage of the event and related news can be found by searching the code R/JA.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LATEST STORIES: \par  \par WSJ: NUCLEAR PLANT EFFORTS FOCUS ON RESTORING POWER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Workers at Japan's stricken Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power complex continued efforts to restore power to its most troubled reactors, while authorities said they would probe higher-than-permitted levels of radioactivity in nearby seawater. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN NUCLEAR AGENCY: FOUND RADIOACTIVE MATERIAL IN SEAWATER NEAR DAIICHI PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Nuclear and Industrial Safety Agency said Tuesday it has again detected radioactive materials in seawater near an outlet at the quake-damaged Fukushima nuclear power plant. (published 0704 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: BOJ FLOODS BANKING SYSTEM WITH RECORD LIQUIDITY TO SUPPORT ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flooded the banking system with a record amount of cash Tuesday to ensure financial institutions have enough liquidity to cope with a spike in demand for funds following the devastating earthquake and counter a yen rise that threatens the economy. (published 0612 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN MAINTAINS THREAT OF FURTHER G-7 ACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials on Tuesday maintained the threat of further yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations, saying joint action is not limited to last week's coordinated market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ECONOMY MINISTER: NUCLEAR ENERGY KEY TO JAPANESE ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Tuesday that nuclear power would remain the primary source of energy for the Japanese economy despite concerns over safety after problems at the quake-hit Fukushima Daiichi power plant. (published 0056 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par QUAKE COULD SPARK BIG CHANGES IN DPJ MANIFESTO - NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan is stepping up moves to drastically change his ruling Democratic Party of Japan's manifesto, or a set of pledges, in a bid to secure funding for reconstruction work after the devastating March 11 earthquake and tsunami, the Nikkei reported in its Tuesday morning edition. (published 0421 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN RELEASES MORE OIL FROM STOCKPILES TO MEET URGENT DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Tuesday it has approved the release of a further 22 days worth of oil reserves in an effort to boost shipments to the quake- and tsunami-stricken northern region. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(3/22) TOKYO SUSPENDS MORE FOOD SHIPMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government moved to prevent tainted agricultural products from reaching consumers, after the number of cases of food and water being contaminated by radioactive materials in northern Japan expanded across a wider area. (published 2333 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(3/22) U.N. AGENCY CALLS FOR SAFETY REVIEW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of the United Nations' nuclear-advisory body said the response to the accident at Japan's Fukushima Daiichi nuclear-power plant has raised questions about the effectiveness of the international nuclear-safety framework. (published 2328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 22-03-11 0723GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110322e73m000h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
