2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy tells Dow Jones that the G7 pledge Friday to conduct joint JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not be considered limited to that day. "It's now a lot harder for speculators to buy the yen, which means for the time being those kinds of speculative moves have likely been suppressed," says Hideaki Inoue, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Mitsubishi UFJ Trust and Banking.(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2344 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/JPY may test 82.00 amid ongoing concerns over the possibility that the Japanese MOF may conduct more JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Hideaki Inoue, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Mitsubishi UFJ Trust and Banking. "I think the trend should be toward a weaker yen for now given the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the moves by the BOJ to ease further, which make it harder for speculators to buy the yen." With speculators sidelined, Inoue says moves will be driven by Japanese exporters, importers and other "real money" players. He says the USD/JPY's support around 80.00 looks solid for now and it's trading at 81.27. The EUR/JPY is at 115.50 and it may rise to 116.00. The EUR/USD is at 1.4206 and it may target 1.4283. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2342 GMT [Dow Jones] The Kospi is tipped to rise, tracking strong gains in U.S. shares following news of a major telecoms deal, while easing concerns over the nuclear crisis in Japan will likely continue to support market sentiment, analysts say; they tip key resistance at the 60-day moving average near 2031. Foreigners' moves in the market will likely be in focus after their three-day buying streak, amid doubts that their buying will develop into a firm trend as uncertainties relating to the unrest in the Middle East and north Africa continue. Analysts cite securities firms and airline stocks as among their top picks following their recent weakness. The Kospi ends up 1.1% at 2003.42 Monday. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com) [ 03-21-11 2032ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110322e73m0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
