\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Yen Could Offer Value, But Caution Warranted As  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Looms\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 02:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, there are still some opportunities--albeit rife with risk--to profit from a run-up in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the dollar hit an all-time low against the yen of Y76.25 Wednesday, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in concert with other Group of Seven industrialized countries' central banks including the Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing the dollar well above Y81.\par \par \uc2 Yet even with the specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , either by a go-it-alone \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or in concert with the country's industrialized peers, an investor still would likely come out ahead on a pro-yen bet, said Pierre Lequeux, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management at Aviva Investors in London. The firm is a unit of \uc2 Aviva PLC\uc2  (AV, AV.LN), which has assets under management of more than $370 billion.\par \par \uc2 The dollar is likely to drop to Y75 within six months, Lequeux said, as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthens from yen-buying by Japanese insurance companies readying to pay out claims, and on yen purchases for rebuilding costs after the earthquake.\par \par \uc2 Many money managers and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists cautioned that given the big risks that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  poses to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants, they'd rather stay away from the yen altogether. But if a client is particularly eager to book quick profits--or if a transaction needs to be done using the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 --the near-term bias is for a stronger yen, said Lequeux.\par \par \uc2 "If you have to make a bet about strong yen or weak yen, I would lean a little bit on the strong-yen side, whilst recognizing it may not be the best payout in terms of risk-adjusted," returns, Lequeux said. "You may get \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from time to time."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely keep on guard for what it deems excessive appreciation, said Constantine Ponticos, managing director of investment management research in London for Pareto, which manages more than $50 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Monday afternoon, the dollar traded at Y81.02 from Y80.59 late Friday, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 "If the yen appreciates from here, I think they will be back in," Ponticos said of Japanese monetary authorities.\par \par \uc2 Overall, Ponticos said Pareto has a small, short yen position. "Even at Y76, the majority of our mandates were still short yen," Ponticos said of client instructions to keep anti-yen bets in place as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped to its all-time low of Y76.25.\par \par \uc2 The coordinated, global \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has "drawn a line in the sand," said Ryan Gibbons, managing partner at GPS, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 -advisory firm in Salt Lake City. The Bank of Japan's tolerance for yen strength is likely the dollar below Y79, but anything below Y80 will get the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's attention, he said.\par \par \uc2 "We continue to push our clients who have benefited from the yen's strength towards hedging at these levels," Gibbons said. Waiting around too long for the yen to strengthen even further before booking profits could cause an investor to get burned by possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. "The old adage that 'Pigs get fed, hogs get slaughtered,' applies here.\par \par \uc2 "I suspect in the weeks and months to come, those who decided to wait will be wishing they had locked in at better levels," he said.\par \par \uc2 For now, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  has not made a strong recommendation on the yen, said Thomas Stolper, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "It's just very difficult to predict," with so many crosscurrents in the market at the moment, Stolper said. The dollar should trade in a wide range, slightly below Y80 to Y86 in the near-term, he said. -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654; bradley.davis@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110323e73m001q2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
