\par\par \b \uc2 CHARTING MARKETS: Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Will Be On The Levels\b0\par\par\uc2 By Stephen Cox, CMT   \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN   \par \uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 22:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The holiday is over. The prospect of more yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't.\par \par \uc2 Monday's spring equinox holiday in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was followed Tuesday by comments from Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda that the Group of Seven is ready to start selling yen again and by news that the Bank of Japan had committed a record Y41.72 trillion in fresh liquidity to the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Clearly, Japan wants the yen to weaken further and feels that the joint actions Friday by the Bank of Japan, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of England and the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  might not have been enough to achieve that. But if they come back, where and when will it happen?\par \par \uc2 If there's a manual on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  out there I haven't read it. But one potentially constructive way to think about the next bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is through technical analysis.\par \par \uc2 For example, weakening the yen relative to the dollar might be accomplished by attacking a prominent resistance level for the dollar. As the dollar tests such a level, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would throw its capital on the buy side to break resistance and push it higher. A decisive break would turn resistance into support thus increasing the relative strength of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 And for that purpose, it makes sense to choose a long-term level because of its "stickiness."\par \par \uc2 The dollar is trading as of this writing at Y80.98. From there, the closest monthly resistance is its May 1995 low of Y81.77. Counterintuitively, then, the G-7 authorities might enter at levels at which the yen is no stronger, but weaker from here.\par \par \uc2 And beyond that Y81.77 figure, the next monthly resistance level for the dollar is Y83.55. Given that Fumihiko Igarashi, one of the two senior Japanese vice finance ministers, said his "desire" is to see the dollar-yen exchange rate at levels seen before the March 11 earthquake and tsunami--a figure around Y83--they might even be tempted to take a shot at turning that resistance into support.\par \par \uc2 -By Stephen Cox, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2212; stephen.cox@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Stephen Cox, a chartered market technician, is chief technician for Dow Jones Newswires.)\par \par \uc2 (Data by CQG)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 03-22-11 1723ET ]\par \par \uc2 1081 4247   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110322e73m000es\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
