\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 774 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 21:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2   TO BUY \f28 \uc2 \f2 T-MOBILE USA\f28 \uc2 \f2  IN $39 BILLION DEAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  is buying \f28 \uc2 \f2 T-Mobile USA\f28 \uc2 \f2  from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Telekom\f28 \uc2 \f2  for $39 billion in cash and stock, a move that would create the nation's largest wireless carrier and shift the competitive landscape of the U.S. industry. \f28 \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares rise 1%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Telekom\f28 \uc2 \f2  ADS's jump 11%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCKS CLIMB; ENERGY LEADS AS OIL PRICES RISE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average climbs back above 12000, after \f28 \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it will buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 T-Mobile USA\f28 \uc2 \f2  for $39 billion and energy companies surge as oil prices leap higher.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US EXISTING-HOME SALES FALL 9.6 % IN FEBRUARY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Existing home sales in the U.S. decline by 9.6% in February to a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 4.88 million, and prices fall to the lowest level in nearly nine years, indications that the market remains depressed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALLIES SHOW DIVISIONS ON LIBYA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. and its allies launch more missile strikes against Col. Moammar Gadhafi and say they will expand the no-fly zone over Libya, as coalition officials work to ease divisions about course of the military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  there.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PROGRESS AT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NUCLEAR PLANT IS SLOW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power\f28 \uc2 \f2  continues to report progress in restoring order at the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear reactors, but finishing the job is turning out to be a painstaking process plagued by damaged equipment and unexpected incidents.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TREASURY\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO START WINDING DOWN  MBS PORTFOLIO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Treasury Department plans to start selling off a $142 billion portfolio of mortgage-backed securities purchased at the height of the financial crisis, winding down a program credited with helping the housing market to stabilize.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL RISES AS AIR STRIKES SPARK SUPPLY WORRIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil futures settle higher as air strikes by the U.S. and its allies in Libya raise concerns about extended oil-supply disruptions amid growing regional tensions. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nymex\f28 \uc2 \f2  April crude settles $1.26, or 1.3%, higher at $102.33 a barrel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANADARKO, \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOREA NATIONAL OIL\f28 \uc2 \f2  IN JOINT VENTURE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anadarko Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it has signed a $1.55 billion joint-venture agreement with state-run \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea National Oil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  ., or KNOC, for one-third of its Maverick Basin assets in southwest Texas.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KEYCORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  , SUNTRUST BORROW TO REPAY TARP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A firmer tone across credit markets is allowing U.S. companies to borrow nearly $6 billion in new deals, including two banks seeking financing to pay back government-bailout funds: \f28 \uc2 \f2 KeyCorp\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 SunTrust Banks\f28 \uc2 \f2  .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FEES TO LEHMAN BANKRUPTCY PROFESSIONALS HIT $1.2B \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The army of bankruptcy lawyers, consultants and financial advisers unwinding investment bank \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers\f28 \uc2 \f2  took in another $29 million last month, as the tab for the most expensive bankruptcy in the U.S. climbed to $1.2 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Analysis \par YEN COULD OFFER VALUE, BUT CAUTION WARRANTED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen, there are still some opportunities -- albeit rife with risk -- to profit from a run-up in the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Bradley Davis writes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Big Picture \par HIGHER INFLATION EXPECTATIONS ARE SPREADING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects higher price pressures to be "transitory," a new survey of finance professionals by \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  shows core inflation expectations are rising around the world, writes Kathleen Madigan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Technically Speaking \par DOLLAR BREAKDOWN ISN'T A BOON FOR STOCKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wall Street investors have cheered a falling dollar over the last few years, but they should think twice before believing that the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent break of a long-term uptrend will be good for the stock market, writes Tomi Kilgore.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Heard on the Street \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2   DEAL COULD BOOST \f28 \uc2 \f2 VERIZON\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Verizon CEO Ivan Seidenberg may feel a bit better about stepping down at the end of the year in the wake of \f28 \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  's deal to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 T-Mobile\f28 \uc2 \f2 , writes Martin Peers, as the deal arguably makes \f28 \uc2 \f2 Verizon Wireless\f28 \uc2 \f2  the winner in the near term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCKS CLIMB, ENERGY LEADS AS OIL PRICES RISE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US stocks climb, boosted by \f28 \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  deal and energy companies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TREASURY\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRICES FALL FURTHER; \f28 \uc2 \f2 TREASURY\f28 \uc2 \f2  DEPT TO SELL MORTGAGES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US Treasurys fall further after Treasury announces MBS sales.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO SLIPS VS DOLLAR AFTER \f28 \uc2 \f2 US TREASURY\f28 \uc2 \f2  NEWS, PORTUGAL FEARS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar gains against euro after Treasury announces MBS sales.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE GAINS AS AIRSTRIKES RAISE SUPPLY WORRIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil futures rise as air strikes against forces in Libya raise supply worries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLD GAINS AMID LIBYA, JAPAN UNCERTAINTY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comex gold rises amid continued uncertainty in Libya and Japan. [ 21-03-11 2000GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110321e73l0016h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
